  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nChronicle of 1st Green Jackets, 43rd and 52nd and The Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1960\n£5.00\n\nLow stock, 3 remaining\nChronicle of 1st Green Jackets, 43rd and 52nd and The Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1960 quantity\nAdd to Cart\n\nCompiled and Edited by Lieutenant-Colonel J. B. Jarvis. Volume LXII January to December 1960.\n\nPublished 1960 - Sydney Lee (Exeter) Ltd. Hardcover.\n\n \n\nContents:\n\nThe Army List September 1960 -p.1\n\nFormer Officers of the Regiment on the Active List -p.3\n\nRegular Officers of the Regiment Extra-Regimentally Employed -p.4\n\nExtracts from the 'London Gazette' -p.5\n\nThe Colonel Commandant -p.11\n\nMajor-General Sir John Winterton's Farewell Address to the 43rd and 52nd -p.12\n\nLetters - General Sir Gerald Lathbury and Major-General Sir John Winterton -p.14\n\nRecords of the 1st Green Jackets, 43rd and 52nd 1960 -p.16\n\nSummary of the 1st Green Jackets, 43rd and 52nd Diary -p.18\n\nCompanies of the 43rd and 52nd 1960 -p.30\n\nFirst Green Jackets, 43rd and 52nd Letter -p.31\n\nFirst Green Jackets, 43rd and 52nd, Records of Sport and Training 1960 -p.35\n\nMessing About In Boats -p.45.\n\nGreen Jackets Brigade Depot Letter -p.48\n\nRegimental Collect - Green Jackets Brigade -p.50\n\nRecords of The Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry (T. A.) -p.51\n\nCompanies of The Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry (T. A.) -p.53\n\nThe Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry (T. A.) Letter -p.54\n\nPronto's Progress -p.58\n\nBuckinghamshire Battalions Old Comrades' Association -p.60\n\nVisit Brigade of Gurkhas Contingent -p.61\n\nVisit of H.M. King of Nepal -p.66\n\nLetters - Major-General L. H. O. Pugh and the Colonel Commandant. Concerning Visit of Brigade of Gurkhas Contingent -p.69\n\nInstallation of General Sir Bernard Paget - G.C.B. -p.71\n\nOfficers Mess Silver and Pictures -p.73\n\nMess Dress -p.77\n\nThe Regiment - A Precis -p.80\n\nLight Infantry Drill -p.83\n\nThe Royal Monmouthshire Militia -p.86\n\nThe Centenary of the Volunteer Force -p.88\n\nCommonwealth Integration -p.94\n\nThe Aden Protectorate Levies -p.99\n\nSomething New  -p.105\n\nImpressions From A Trip To Poland -p.108\n\nL'Apres-Ski -p.115\n\nCairngorm Expedition -p.118\n\nAround the Lake in Fourteen Days -p.121\n\nLight Division 150th Anniversary Luncheon -p.137\n\nRegimental Dinner -p.141\n\n43rd Light Infantry Mesopotamian Luncheon-p.142\n\n43rd Light Infantry Dinner (Second World War) -p.143\n\n52nd Light Infantry Dinner (First World War) -p.144\n\n52nd Light Infantry Dinner (Second World War) -p.145\n\nRoll of 43rd Officers -p.146\n\nTwo East Anglian Memorials -p.148\n\nOccasional Notes -p. 150\n\nObituaries -p.151\n\nPlease Note: Original copies supplied, all in used but reasonable condition. Copy supplied may vary slightly from the one pictured in terms of wear and aging.\n\n \n\nRelated products\nThe Skipper’s War: Dragon School, Oxford & The Great War\n£20.00 Add to cart\nBugle & Sabre III\n£5.00 Read more\nBugle & Sabre XI\n£4.99 Add to cart\nBugle & Sabre VIII\n£5.00 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
